188
00:13:54,477 --> 00:13:55,157
[SPEAKER_00]: How old is she?

189
00:13:55,457 --> 00:13:56,998
[SPEAKER_00]: She should be 87.

190
00:13:58,199 --> 00:14:01,320
[SPEAKER_00]: And every other year, see, we go back there.

191
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:03,701
[SPEAKER_00]: Now this year, my brother's come out here.

192
00:14:04,698 --> 00:14:11,081
[SPEAKER_00]: But when I went back last year, and we went up to see her, and she just talked us aspry.

193
00:14:11,121 --> 00:14:15,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Then the next time you go up and talk to her, doesn't remember.

194
00:14:15,243 --> 00:14:17,404
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just one of those things.

195
00:14:18,785 --> 00:14:30,590
[SPEAKER_00]: But now this past, my sister just called, and she says, nobody's allowed in a nursing home for two weeks.

196
00:14:30,810 --> 00:14:31,651
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, so how come?

197
00:14:33,161 --> 00:14:35,523
[SPEAKER_00]: And she said, well, kind of this flu epidemic.

198
00:14:36,704 --> 00:14:39,045
[SPEAKER_00]: And I said, well, I think that's a pretty good idea.

199
00:14:39,846 --> 00:14:47,011
