1207
01:15:12,851 --> 01:15:19,412
[SPEAKER_00]: Them people in there, they liked me as much as if I was playing for Brooklyn.

1208
01:15:19,473 --> 01:15:19,793
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

1209
01:15:19,973 --> 01:15:20,533
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know.

1210
01:15:21,253 --> 01:15:25,974
[SPEAKER_00]: They always, I mean they'd always come down, talk to me, shake my hand, everything.

1211
01:15:26,954 --> 01:15:28,214
[SPEAKER_00]: They just loved me, I guess.

1212
01:15:29,395 --> 01:15:33,756
[SPEAKER_00]: And this band that they always had in there, they'd always play that Dago song.

1213
01:15:34,616 --> 01:15:37,157
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I tell you, it was a card.

1214
01:15:37,977 --> 01:15:39,117
[SPEAKER_00]: It really was a card.

1215
01:15:40,776 --> 01:15:42,257
[SPEAKER_00]: But I enjoyed playing over there.

1216
01:15:42,337 --> 01:15:43,577
[SPEAKER_02]: Is that your favorite ballpark?

1217
01:15:43,797 --> 01:15:45,518
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I really liked that ballpark.

1218
01:15:46,138 --> 01:15:48,459
[SPEAKER_02]: You never played in Baker Bowl, did you, in Philadelphia?

1219
01:15:48,479 --> 01:15:48,899
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah.

1220
01:15:49,439 --> 01:15:49,899
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, did you?

1221
01:15:50,140 --> 01:15:51,440
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yes, we played down there.

1222
01:15:53,501 --> 01:15:56,222
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, that was kind of a comfortable right field, wasn't it?

1223
01:15:56,262 --> 01:15:57,442
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, my goodness.

1224
01:15:57,462 --> 01:15:59,363
[SPEAKER_02]: For batting, I don't know about playing out there.

1225
01:16:00,263 --> 01:16:03,125
[SPEAKER_00]: And they sure played a tattoo on that thing.

1226
01:16:03,785 --> 01:16:05,005
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah, Baker Bowl.

1227
01:16:05,646 --> 01:16:06,686
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, we played there in 40.

1228
01:16:08,012 --> 01:16:12,175
[SPEAKER_00]: I think 40 and 41 I think we played there, and then in 42 I think they went over to...

1229
01:16:12,435 --> 01:16:16,218
[SPEAKER_00]: I was thinking they went over earlier, but... No, no, they played down there.

1230
01:16:17,839 --> 01:16:23,363
[SPEAKER_00]: I know when Chuck, Chuck Klein, he was down there in this Boom Boom Beck.

1231
01:16:23,383 --> 01:16:24,504
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, Boom Boom Beck.

1232
01:16:24,544 --> 01:16:27,746
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh boy, he was something.

1233
01:16:27,766 --> 01:16:29,287
[SPEAKER_02]: I wish I could have seen that old ball.

1234
01:16:30,648 --> 01:16:33,430
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, there's a funny story about this Boom Boom Beck.

1235
01:16:34,251 --> 01:16:36,132
[SPEAKER_00]: Chuck Klein, you know, he's playing right field.

1236
01:16:39,406 --> 01:16:41,608
[SPEAKER_00]: They were hitting him pretty good, this boom-boom back.

1237
01:16:41,989 --> 01:16:46,933
[SPEAKER_00]: The manager, you know, he come out and was gonna take him out of the ballgame, you know.

1238
01:16:46,953 --> 01:17:00,927
[SPEAKER_00]: And he was so mad that he threw that ball up against that right field fence, you know, and, you know, Chuck Bryant was down like that, you know, and he thought the ballgame, you know, was hollered, you know.

1239
01:17:00,987 --> 01:17:02,328
[SPEAKER_00]: And when he heard that thing hit,

1240
01:17:03,017 --> 01:17:04,977
[SPEAKER_00]: He looked around there and he seen that ball.

1241
01:17:05,017 --> 01:17:08,898
[SPEAKER_00]: He run over there and retrieved the ball and threw it in there so fast, you know.

1242
01:17:09,798 --> 01:17:13,139
[SPEAKER_00]: And it finally dawned on him, boom, boom, Beck threw the ball.

1243
01:17:13,879 --> 01:17:16,319
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, it was something.

1244
01:17:18,300 --> 01:17:20,440
[SPEAKER_02]: What's some of the funniest things that happened?

1245
01:17:20,460 --> 01:17:22,880
[SPEAKER_02]: Can you think of anything on the ball field in any of your experience?

1246
01:17:23,300 --> 01:17:32,102
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, well, it's, well, boom, boom, Beck, he was, when we played him in Philadelphia, you know, it's Clyde McCullough.

1247
01:17:34,089 --> 01:17:39,053
[SPEAKER_00]: He seen him warming up, and he grabbed three, four bats.

1248
01:17:39,073 --> 01:17:40,735
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, let me at it, let me at it.

1249
01:17:40,775 --> 01:17:43,697
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, boy, he says, I know that's one guy I can hit.

1250
01:17:44,938 --> 01:17:49,462
[SPEAKER_00]: And I looked at him, I said, Clyde, he says, you can't hit that guy.

1251
01:17:49,482 --> 01:17:50,743
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, nobody can hit him.

1252
01:17:52,264 --> 01:17:57,809
[SPEAKER_00]: And sure enough, he goes up there and boom, boom, back, struck him out three straight times.

1253
01:17:58,690 --> 01:17:59,891
[SPEAKER_00]: And we said to him, he says,

1254
01:18:01,719 --> 01:18:02,780
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to go up and hit again?

1255
01:18:02,840 --> 01:18:04,961
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, nope, I don't want to hit against that guy.

1256
01:18:05,722 --> 01:18:09,124
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he'd give you, he'd get you off balance.

1257
01:18:10,185 --> 01:18:14,849
[SPEAKER_00]: Either way, when you're looking for the slow one, he'd throw the fast one by you.

1258
01:18:14,909 --> 01:18:17,470
[SPEAKER_00]: And when you're looking for the fast one, he'd just throw the slow one by you.

1259
01:18:18,431 --> 01:18:22,714
[SPEAKER_00]: And I'm telling you, he had you in stitches just to watch you pitch.

1260
01:18:25,156 --> 01:18:30,600
[SPEAKER_00]: Then another thing, another good one was when I was with the Red Sox, this Wes Farrell,

1261
01:18:31,740 --> 01:18:32,501
[SPEAKER_00]: the picture, you know.

1262
01:18:33,741 --> 01:18:35,382
[SPEAKER_00]: We were in Comiskey Park.

1263
01:18:35,742 --> 01:18:39,644
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, their dugout ain't any higher than this.

1264
01:18:40,265 --> 01:18:48,709
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you stand up, you know, you hit your head up against the cement ceiling there, you know.

1265
01:18:48,789 --> 01:18:55,553
[SPEAKER_00]: So something come up, and this West Farrell, he jumped up, you know, and the next thing you know,

1266
01:18:56,943 --> 01:19:03,708
[SPEAKER_00]: Everybody jumped up, you know, because I don't know who it was that got the base hit or something, you know, and we were rallying and winning the ball game, see.

1267
01:19:04,428 --> 01:19:07,970
[SPEAKER_00]: Next thing you know, we looked over there and here he is laying down, you know.

1268
01:19:09,311 --> 01:19:11,353
[SPEAKER_00]: Somebody says, well, what's the matter with Wes?

1269
01:19:12,433 --> 01:19:14,515
[SPEAKER_00]: And they finally looked at him, he was knocked out.

1270
01:19:15,635 --> 01:19:20,619
[SPEAKER_00]: And they revised him, you know, and said, well, what happened?

1271
01:19:20,659 --> 01:19:23,661
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, oh, these dugouts, you know, he says,

1272
01:19:24,480 --> 01:19:32,381
[SPEAKER_00]: jumped up and forgot what I was doing, and I hit my head up against that, and he just knocked him out, just knocked him out cold.

1273
01:19:32,401 --> 01:19:33,442
[SPEAKER_02]: That's in Comiskey Park.

1274
01:19:33,702 --> 01:19:33,962
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

1275
01:19:35,482 --> 01:19:40,583
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, it was just, oh, I mean, their dugout over there, it was pitiful.

1276
01:19:41,603 --> 01:19:43,543
[SPEAKER_00]: Then another funny one happened.

1277
01:19:44,483 --> 01:19:48,404
[SPEAKER_00]: We played up there with the Boston Braves, you know.

1278
01:19:48,924 --> 01:19:51,705
[SPEAKER_00]: That's a ballpark they had up there.

1279
01:19:55,619 --> 01:19:57,840
[SPEAKER_00]: They have the dugout, see, and that's a deep one.

1280
01:19:59,081 --> 01:20:01,523
[SPEAKER_00]: And when you stand there, you can just about see over it.

1281
01:20:01,783 --> 01:20:07,327
[SPEAKER_00]: And, well, I made the last out this one time.

1282
01:20:07,447 --> 01:20:16,433
[SPEAKER_00]: And instead of running all the way in to the dugout, I just went under the stands there because the clubhouse is right under the stands, see.

1283
01:20:16,453 --> 01:20:18,134
[SPEAKER_00]: And I went over there and smoked a cigarette.

1284
01:20:19,595 --> 01:20:23,157
[SPEAKER_00]: And after the inning was over, you know, I run out left field.

1285
01:20:25,086 --> 01:20:34,148
[SPEAKER_00]: Pretty soon, I was down on my haunches, like, you know, and waiting for Claude Pasol, you know, to start pitching, you know.

1286
01:20:34,208 --> 01:20:37,169
[SPEAKER_00]: And pretty soon, Charlie Grimm comes running out.

1287
01:20:38,389 --> 01:20:39,809
[SPEAKER_00]: And Beans Reddin there again.

1288
01:20:40,569 --> 01:20:41,649
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, what's the matter?

1289
01:20:42,490 --> 01:20:44,350
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, I don't have a left fielder.

1290
01:20:46,050 --> 01:20:47,031
[SPEAKER_00]: Beans looked out there.

1291
01:20:47,051 --> 01:20:48,751
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, well, Dominick's out there.

1292
01:20:50,191 --> 01:20:53,492
[SPEAKER_00]: And so they finally started the game, you know.

1293
01:20:54,806 --> 01:21:01,209
[SPEAKER_00]: I come into the dugout, you know, and Charlie says to me, he says, crying out loud, he says, will you stand up so I can see you?

1294
01:21:02,350 --> 01:21:10,134
[SPEAKER_00]: He thought I wasn't out there, you know, he thought we only had eight ballplayers out there.

1295
01:21:10,194 --> 01:21:11,094
[SPEAKER_02]: You were kneeling down?

1296
01:21:11,374 --> 01:21:18,938
[SPEAKER_00]: No, I was, you know, I had my hands on my, bent over like, is what it was, you know, so he couldn't see me out there.

1297
01:21:19,328 --> 01:21:20,829
[SPEAKER_00]: Now if I'd have been standing up for it.

1298
01:21:21,029 --> 01:21:22,789
[SPEAKER_00]: They're so low down, I mean the angle.

1299
01:21:22,809 --> 01:21:23,230
[SPEAKER_00]: That is right.

1300
01:21:23,830 --> 01:21:25,210
[SPEAKER_00]: The angle was hard to see.

1301
01:21:25,530 --> 01:21:27,511
[SPEAKER_00]: And the kind of the dugout being so low.

1302
01:21:28,111 --> 01:21:31,933
[SPEAKER_00]: And boy he'd come out of that.

1303
01:21:33,794 --> 01:21:35,794
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you get along pretty well with umpires?

1304
01:21:36,475 --> 01:21:36,895
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh yeah.

1305
01:21:37,835 --> 01:21:39,996
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh there's another funny one.

1306
01:21:40,196 --> 01:21:42,757
[SPEAKER_00]: The first time I was ever thrown out of a big league ball game.

1307
01:21:43,417 --> 01:21:44,358
[SPEAKER_00]: One and only time.

1308
01:21:45,198 --> 01:21:46,338
[SPEAKER_00]: It was over in Cincinnati.

1309
01:21:49,262 --> 01:21:55,806
[SPEAKER_00]: Major Kirk was the umpire behind the plate, and boy, he was, he couldn't pronounce names or anything.

1310
01:21:57,087 --> 01:22:04,032
[SPEAKER_00]: But anyway, in the meantime, Jimmy Wilson was thrown out of the ballgame, and it was one of these heated games, you know.

1311
01:22:05,713 --> 01:22:14,499
[SPEAKER_00]: So all the ballplayers are calling him Meathead, and he come over there, and he says, anytime somebody says that again, he's going to be thrown out of the ballgame.

1312
01:22:15,780 --> 01:22:18,642
[SPEAKER_00]: So Dick Spalding is the acting manager now.

1313
01:22:19,046 --> 01:22:21,187
[SPEAKER_00]: when Wilson was thrown out, see.

1314
01:22:21,807 --> 01:22:29,970
[SPEAKER_00]: And we're up on a little ledge like, because it was a closed ball game and he's discussing with me, I was gonna be the pinch hitter, see.

1315
01:22:31,771 --> 01:22:35,193
[SPEAKER_00]: And we're deciding how we were gonna do this, see.

1316
01:22:35,833 --> 01:22:39,154
[SPEAKER_00]: In the meantime, they holler, I'm out of the ball game.

1317
01:22:39,554 --> 01:22:41,935
[SPEAKER_00]: And I'm discussing this with Dick Spalding, you know.

1318
01:22:43,696 --> 01:22:46,237
[SPEAKER_00]: And this bar,

1319
01:22:47,075 --> 01:22:51,240
[SPEAKER_00]: He'd come running over there, you know, he says, hey, Dallas Sander, he says, you're out of the ballgame.

1320
01:22:51,780 --> 01:22:54,003
[SPEAKER_00]: And I looked up and I says, for what?

1321
01:22:55,885 --> 01:22:57,166
[SPEAKER_00]: I says, I never done anything.

1322
01:22:57,206 --> 01:22:58,988
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm in here talking with Spalding.

1323
01:22:59,749 --> 01:23:02,352
[SPEAKER_00]: And Spalding come out there and he starts raising.

1324
01:23:03,513 --> 01:23:08,879
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, he and I were talking, discussing what we're going to do when it comes time for us to be up the bat.

1325
01:23:11,257 --> 01:23:14,979
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, well, Major Kurth called your name, you're out of the ballgame.

1326
01:23:15,159 --> 01:23:17,401
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, he couldn't even pronounce my name.

1327
01:23:18,742 --> 01:23:28,528
[SPEAKER_00]: So I come up there, me being as small as I am, and Major Kurth so big, I looked up at him, I said, Major Kurth, why did you throw me out of the game?

1328
01:23:30,529 --> 01:23:33,271
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, your name come to my mind first.

1329
01:23:33,651 --> 01:23:37,854
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, you can't even pronounce my name, let alone hollering it over there.

1330
01:23:39,074 --> 01:23:40,035
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, well, he says,

1331
01:23:41,342 --> 01:23:42,343
[SPEAKER_00]: you're out of the ballgame.

1332
01:23:42,363 --> 01:23:44,024
[SPEAKER_00]: And boy, I started letting him do it.

1333
01:23:45,605 --> 01:23:48,308
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, if you don't get out of here, he said, I'll bite your head off.

1334
01:23:49,008 --> 01:23:53,332
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, if you do, you'll have more brains in your stomach than you've got in your head.

1335
01:23:53,972 --> 01:23:54,873
[SPEAKER_00]: And I walked off.

1336
01:23:55,794 --> 01:23:57,115
[SPEAKER_00]: And he couldn't figure that out.

1337
01:23:57,135 --> 01:24:00,337
[SPEAKER_00]: He just couldn't figure what that was, you know.

1338
01:24:01,218 --> 01:24:09,865
[SPEAKER_00]: But anyway, I get in the clubhouse, and Charlie, I mean, Wilson, he said, what are you doing in here?

1339
01:24:10,340 --> 01:24:12,761
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, the closed ball game, you're going to be the pinch hitter.

1340
01:24:12,801 --> 01:24:14,182
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, yeah, that's what I thought.

1341
01:24:15,122 --> 01:24:17,023
[SPEAKER_00]: I said, Major Curt just threw me out of the game.

1342
01:24:17,043 --> 01:24:17,943
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, well, what for?

1343
01:24:17,983 --> 01:24:20,604
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, my name come to his mind first.

1344
01:24:22,285 --> 01:24:26,627
[SPEAKER_00]: And boy, he come out of there, and he says, I'm going to protest this game.

1345
01:24:26,687 --> 01:24:28,407
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, if it's the last thing I do.

1346
01:24:29,768 --> 01:24:32,049
[SPEAKER_00]: Major Curt said, you're out of this ball game.

1347
01:24:32,089 --> 01:24:33,450
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, you can't protest.

1348
01:24:33,870 --> 01:24:35,911
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, don't tell me I can't.

1349
01:24:35,931 --> 01:24:39,312
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, you're throwing one of my ball players out, supposed to be a pinch hitter.

1350
01:24:40,222 --> 01:24:46,527
[SPEAKER_00]: In a close ball game like this here, he says, and he never done anything, he says, I'm protesting.

1351
01:24:47,508 --> 01:24:48,469
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all there is to it.

1352
01:24:48,709 --> 01:24:49,790
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, come on, Dominick.

1353
01:24:49,810 --> 01:24:50,530
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, let's go.

1354
01:24:51,731 --> 01:24:54,253
[SPEAKER_00]: But fortunately, we won the ball game.

1355
01:24:54,493 --> 01:24:55,294
[SPEAKER_02]: That'd be interesting.

1356
01:24:55,634 --> 01:24:58,276
[SPEAKER_00]: What a manager thrown out of a game protesting.

1357
01:24:58,496 --> 01:25:00,318
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course, Spalding could have protested anyhow.

1358
01:25:00,378 --> 01:25:01,499
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah.

1359
01:25:01,539 --> 01:25:03,060
[SPEAKER_00]: He had Spalding up there.

1360
01:25:03,400 --> 01:25:06,683
[SPEAKER_00]: He had him up there, but it was the idea of it, see.

1361
01:25:07,438 --> 01:25:14,220
[SPEAKER_00]: that throwing a man out that never done anything, just because they would call him meathead, and he didn't like that name, see.

1362
01:25:15,140 --> 01:25:24,743
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, everybody on the bench like Paso and Vern Olson and all them guys, you know, they kept agitating him all the time.

1363
01:25:25,203 --> 01:25:27,724
[SPEAKER_00]: But that was just one of those things.

1364
01:25:28,084 --> 01:25:29,865
[SPEAKER_02]: Maybe he was thinking you were

1365
01:25:30,634 --> 01:25:34,615
[SPEAKER_02]: not going to be in the game, you would do least harm putting you out.

1366
01:25:34,635 --> 01:25:35,756
[SPEAKER_02]: He had to put somebody out.

1367
01:25:35,816 --> 01:25:40,897
[SPEAKER_00]: No, he knew that I was going to be the pincher.

1368
01:25:41,378 --> 01:25:42,198
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, he knew that.

1369
01:25:42,758 --> 01:25:44,639
[SPEAKER_00]: And he figured that's a good way to get even with them.

1370
01:25:45,919 --> 01:25:49,380
[SPEAKER_00]: I think that's why he done that.

1371
01:25:49,680 --> 01:25:51,681
[SPEAKER_02]: Would umpires do things like that?

1372
01:25:52,641 --> 01:25:53,602
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, when you get them mad.

1373
01:25:53,982 --> 01:25:56,843
[SPEAKER_00]: Now there's one thing, now there's Beans Red, he's all together different.

1374
01:25:58,183 --> 01:26:00,344
[SPEAKER_00]: We were behind I think nine or ten

1375
01:26:01,299 --> 01:26:02,900
[SPEAKER_00]: runs.

1376
01:26:02,980 --> 01:26:07,044
[SPEAKER_00]: And I kept calling Bean just about everything I could think of.

1377
01:26:08,064 --> 01:26:15,590
[SPEAKER_00]: And I get up to the bat, you know, and he looked at me and he said, Hey, Dago, he says, I got to be in, I got to stay out here and umpire this ball game.

1378
01:26:15,610 --> 01:26:17,552
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, you're going to stay right here with me.

1379
01:26:18,253 --> 01:26:19,894
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, I'm not going to throw you out of this.

1380
01:26:21,315 --> 01:26:29,942
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just, I mean, his humor was like, you couldn't, I mean, you could talk to him and he'd never bother you.

1381
01:26:31,648 --> 01:26:32,768
[SPEAKER_00]: He had real good humor.

1382
01:26:33,669 --> 01:26:37,429
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, if all umpires were like him, it'd be all right.

1383
01:26:38,390 --> 01:26:40,810
[SPEAKER_00]: They wouldn't have no trouble at all.

1384
01:26:40,830 --> 01:26:43,491
[SPEAKER_02]: How about Bill Clem?

1385
01:26:44,131 --> 01:26:44,971
[SPEAKER_00]: He was a marvel.

1386
01:26:45,812 --> 01:26:48,352
[SPEAKER_00]: He'd get that foot and he'd draw a line.

1387
01:26:49,553 --> 01:26:51,633
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, don't you come over that line.

1388
01:26:51,673 --> 01:26:53,754
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, if you do, you know where you're going.

1389
01:26:54,874 --> 01:26:57,935
[SPEAKER_00]: And brother, I'll tell you, there's nobody ever went over that line.

1390
